messages:
nora-docs: Heads-up 1 I'm opening a small PR to propose a compact 'envelope-lite' pattern for function/tool returns in structured-output docs. Goal: reduce parser footguns in tutorials while giving a clear migration path. Need quick JS+Py shim snippets and a before/after we can paste into the guide.

eli-ml: +1. Please call out the exact pain cases: singleton vs array, optional keys omitted vs null, and how to represent union items.

nora-docs: Draft rules (in PR body):
- Top-level `envelope_lite` object with keys: `kind`, `v` (short for version), `items` (always array).
- Optional `meta` for provenance.
- Prefer explicit nulls instead of omitting expected fields.
- Keep the shape compact so examples remain readable.

sam-devex: We'll need compatibility shims for older `result`/raw-array shapes that people copy from tutorials. Small, copy-paste friendly snippets are best. Also include a unit-test suggestion for SDKs: assert normalize(...).items is always a list.

fran-ux: UX ask: show a before/after diff and a one-line rationale: "arrays = predictable iteration + easier batching". Also show a consumer loop snippet.

nora-docs: Draft before/after for the guide: 
```json
// BEFORE (ambiguous)
{ "result": { "text": "ok" } }

// AFTER (envelope_lite)
{
  "envelope_lite": {
    "kind": "tool_resp",
    "v": "1",
    "items": [ { "text": "ok" } ],
    "meta": { "model": "redwood-small" }
  }
}
```

eli-ml: For union items suggest including a discriminator field per item (e.g. `type`) and show an example: `{ "type": "file", "path": "/tmp/x" }`. Also note that `items: [{"note": null}]` beats dropping `note`.

sam-devex: JS shim (very small, to include in SDK docs):
```js
// normalizeEnvelopeLite -> { kind, v, items: [] }
function normalizeEnvelopeLite(resp){
  if(resp?.envelope_lite?.items) return resp.envelope_lite;
  if(Array.isArray(resp)) return { kind: 'legacy_array', v: '0', items: resp };
  if(resp?.result) return { kind: 'legacy_result', v: '0', items: Array.isArray(resp.result) ? resp.result : [resp.result] };
  return { kind: 'unknown', v: '0', items: [] };
}
```

fran-ux: Add a tiny consumer loop example after that: `for (const it of normalized.items) { /* handle it */ }` and a note: "If item has `type`, switch on it."

sam-devex: Python shim: 
```py
# normalize_envelope_lite -> {'kind': str, 'v': str, 'items': list}
def normalize_envelope_lite(resp):
    if resp and isinstance(resp.get('envelope_lite'), dict) and isinstance(resp['envelope_lite'].get('items'), list):
        return resp['envelope_lite']
    if isinstance(resp, list):
        return {'kind': 'legacy_array', 'v': '0', 'items': resp}
    if resp and 'result' in resp:
        r = resp['result']
        return {'kind': 'legacy_result', 'v': '0', 'items': r if isinstance(r, list) else [r]}
    return {'kind': 'unknown', 'v': '0', 'items': []}
```

eli-ml: Suggest adding a short JSON Schema snippet we can run in CI to validate examples in the docs (schema: envelope_lite object with items: array). That will catch commas/typos.

nora-docs: Good idea. I'll add a simple schema check step to the docs build for the examples folder. Also adding a migration checklist to the PR body: update tutorial examples, add shim snippets to SDK snippets page, grep for "result" and plan staged updates, and add a small note in the changelog.

ci-bot: PR opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5219 - "Envelope_lite: compact envelope + SDK shims" by nora-docs. Docs build: examples schema check passed.

sam-devex: I'll copy the JS normalize into our client utils and add a unit test (assert items is list and preserves item types).

fran-ux: Tiny wording nit: call the field `v` "v (short for version)" in the docs so it's clear. Also include a tiny example of handling `truncated` via meta if we need it later.

nora-docs: Thanks, folding those in. Plan: merge tomorrow afternoon if no objections. Tagging @eli-ml and @sam-devex for final signoff. :rocket:
